   2	 * Reading flow from the rhythm of the keys.
   3	 *
   4	 * Nothing here looks at the words — only at when they arrive and how many are
   5	 * taken back. Five readings:
   6	 *
   7	 *   away      no keys for minutes; nothing should change around the page
   8	 *   working   ordinary writing: pauses, rereads, small cuts
   9	 *   settling  a steady run has begun; the chrome starts to dim
  10	 *   flow      the run has held; the room goes quiet and the page stands alone
  11	 *   stuck     a long pause after cutting and circling — help may land now
  12	 *
  13	 * The readings are sticky on purpose. Entering flow takes a sustained run;
  14	 * leaving it takes a real pause (or the writer reaching for the room), never
  15	 * a single deletion or a glance away. A rewrite inside flow is still flow.
  16	 *
  17	 * Thresholds are not constants: `thresholdsFor` in `flow-profile.ts` derives
  18	 * them from how this writer actually pauses. Pure — `now` is passed in.
  19	 */
